  "helpCallManagementText": "Calling & In-Call Controls",
  "@helpCallManagementText": {
    "description": "Help: text in an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementIntro": "SreerajP Contacts Sphere provides an intelligent calling experience with multi-party controls, dual-SIM management, automatic redial assistance, and spoken caller announcements.",
  "@helpCallManagementIntro": {
    "description": "Help: lead paragraph of an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementTitle1": "In-Call Controls & Conference Calling",
  "@helpCallManagementTitle1": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet1": "Mute & Speaker: Tap Mute to silence your microphone, or Speaker for loud hands-free audio.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet1": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet2": "Hold & Keypad: Put active calls on hold or open the dialpad to enter IVR menu digits (like pressing 1 for English).",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet2": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet3": "Add Call & Call Swap: Add a second participant while keeping the first call on hold. Tap Swap to switch between active callers.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet3": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet4": "Conference Merge: Tap Merge to combine both calls into one conference call. Merge only appears when your network supports conference calls. Tap Manage to see who is on the call, drop one person, or talk to one person in private.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet4": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementTitle2": "Speed Dial",
  "@helpCallManagementTitle2": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet5": "Keypad keys 1 to 9 can each hold one person. Hold a key on the dialer to call them.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet5": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet6": "Holding only works when the number box is empty, so a long press while you are typing never starts a call.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet6": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet7": "To set a key: hold an empty key on the dialer and pick a contact, or go to Settings → Speed Dial. If the contact has more than one number you are asked which one to save.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet7": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet8": "A key that holds someone shows a small coloured dot above the digit.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet8": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet9": "Secret contacts cannot be put on a key, and a key is freed automatically if you delete its contact or make it secret.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet9": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementTitle3": "Dual-SIM Calling & Preferences",
  "@helpCallManagementTitle3": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet10": "On dual-SIM phones, the dialer gives you SIM 1 and SIM 2 call buttons for immediate selection.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet10": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet11": "Settings → SIM & calling → SIM Cards & Accounts sets the default SIM for outgoing calls, or switches on \"Ask before each call\" so you are asked every time.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet11": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet12": "One person can have their own SIM: open the contact, tap Edit, and choose it under \"Preferred SIM\". Calls to them then use that SIM instead of the default one.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet12": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet13": "With \"Ask before each call\" switched on you are still asked, but the SIM that call would have used is already ticked, so it is one tap.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet13": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet14": "If that SIM is later removed from the phone, calls quietly fall back to your default SIM.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet14": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet15": "The same screen gives each SIM its own colour, so you can tell at a glance which line a call is on.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet15": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet16": "Recents shows which SIM was used for each incoming, outgoing, or missed call.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet16": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementTitle4": "Smart Redial & \"Reach Me\" SMS",
  "@helpCallManagementTitle4": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet17": "When an outgoing call is busy or unanswered, the app offers to redial the number for you after a delay.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet17": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet18": "You can instead send a preset \"Reach Me\" text in one tap, to say you tried to get through.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet18": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet19": "Settings → SIM & calling → Smart Redial & \"Reach Me\" sets the default retry delay and the preset message, and lists the redials that are waiting to run.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet19": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet20": "A scheduled redial is the one place the app dials on its own, and only because you set the delay yourself. Cancel a waiting redial from that same list.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet20": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementTitle5": "Spoken Caller Announcements",
  "@helpCallManagementTitle5": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet21": "Turn it on under Settings → SIM & calling → Spoken caller announcement. The app then says the caller's name over the ringtone — \"Amma calling\".",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet21": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet22": "A Malayalam name is announced in Malayalam. Use the Test button on that screen to hear how a name sounds before a real call arrives.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet22": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet23": "Switch on the quiet-hours exception, and set its time range, to stay silent at night while the phone still rings.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet23": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementTitle6": "Quick SMS Decline Replies",
  "@helpCallManagementTitle6": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet24": "Cannot answer right now? Tap Reply on the incoming call screen to decline the call and send a preset text instead.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet24": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementBullet25": "Write your own messages under Settings → SIM & calling → Quick replies.",
  "@helpCallManagementBullet25": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpCallManagementFooter": "Tip: make this your Default Phone App — Settings → Permissions shows whether it already is. Without that role, Android does not hand over the in-call controls or the full-screen incoming alert.",
  "@helpCallManagementFooter": {
    "description": "Help: closing tip of an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesText1": "Relationship categories",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesText1": {
    "description": "Help: text in an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesIntro": "Every relationship you save has two parts: a category and a label. The category is one of seven fixed buckets. The label is whatever you want to call it — \"Father\", \"Cousin Brother\", \"Manager\".",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesIntro": {
    "description": "Help: lead paragraph of an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle1": "Why categories exist",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle1": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet1": "The sphere used to draw one node for every different label. With twenty or more links it turned into a crowd.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet1": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet2": "Now the sphere draws at most seven nodes — one per category. The number inside a node is how many contacts sit in it.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet2": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet3": "Tap a node to see everyone inside it, each with their own label. Nothing is hidden; it is only tidier.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet3": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle2": "Adding a relationship",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle2": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet4": "Pick the contact you want to link.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet4": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet5": "Pick one of the seven categories.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet5": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet6": "Type the label, or tap one of the suggested chips. The chips are only shortcuts — any wording you like is accepted.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet6": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle3": "The seven categories",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle3": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle4": "Both sides, one category",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle4": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet7": "A link is saved on both contacts. If you save someone as your Father, you show up on their side as their Son or Daughter.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet7": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet8": "The reverse side keeps the same category, so the pair always sits in the same bucket on both spheres.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet8": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle5": "Relationships you saved earlier",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle5": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet9": "Old links had no category. On the first launch after this update, each one is sorted by its label — \"Father\" goes to Immediate Family, \"Colleague\" to Professional, and so on.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet9": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet10": "A label the app does not recognise goes to Social. Nothing is deleted, and you can move any link to another category by tapping it and choosing \"Change\".",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet10": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle6": "Quiet hours use these categories",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesTitle6": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet11": "Settings → SIM & calling → Relationship-tier quiet hours silences calls between the times you set.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet11": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet12": "It is an allow list, not a block list. Everyone is silenced except the people you add — starred contacts, whole categories such as Immediate Family, a tag, or named individuals.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet12": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet13": "This is why the category matters: allowing \"Immediate Family\" lets every contact in that bucket ring through, whatever label you gave each one.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesBullet13": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpRelationshipCategoriesFooter": "Tip: if you are unsure where someone belongs, pick the category you would look under later. The label carries the detail.",
  "@helpRelationshipCategoriesFooter": {
    "description": "Help: closing tip of an article. Help prose."
  },

  "helpP2pSyncText": "Sync to Another Device",
  "@helpP2pSyncText": {
    "description": "Help: text in an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncIntro": "Copy your contacts (and more) from one phone to another over the same Wi-Fi network. There is no internet, cloud, or account involved — the two phones talk directly to each other. Both phones must be running this app.",
  "@helpP2pSyncIntro": {
    "description": "Help: lead paragraph of an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle1": "Before you start",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle1": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet1": "Put both phones on the same Wi-Fi network.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet1": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet2": "Make sure both phones run the same version of this app. If the versions do not match, sync stops and asks you to update both phones.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet2": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet3": "On both phones open Settings → Sync to Another Device. It asks for your fingerprint, face, or PIN first, because a sync can include secret contacts.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet3": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet4": "On the phone that is sending, tap \"Send to Another Device\". On the phone that is receiving, tap \"Receive from Another Device\".",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet4": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle2": "How the two phones connect",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle2": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet5": "The sending phone shows a pairing code and a QR code.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet5": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet6": "The receiving phone scans that QR code, or you type the pairing code in by hand.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet6": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet7": "The pairing code is only ever shown on screen — it is never sent over the network. The whole transfer is encrypted using that code, so if the wrong code is used the connection simply fails.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet7": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle3": "Full Sync vs Selective Sync",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle3": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet8": "Full Sync sends everything below in one go. The sender's app settings replace the receiver's, and the sender's own profile (\"Self\") card is added to the receiver as a normal contact (it never replaces the receiver's own profile).",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet8": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet9": "Selective Sync sends only the groups of data you pick. Contacts are always included. Settings only fill in blanks (they never overwrite what the receiver already set), and the sender's \"Self\" card is not sent.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet9": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle4": "What gets synced",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle4": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet10": "Contacts and their details: phone numbers, emails, addresses, official details, social links, and tags.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet10": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet11": "Contact photos and calling-card photos.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet11": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet12": "Call history: call logs, interactions, and reminders.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet12": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet13": "Groups and who belongs to them.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet13": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet14": "Relationships between contacts.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet14": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet15": "Blocked numbers.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet15": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet16": "Your emergency info card — on a Full Sync, or when you tick it while choosing what to share. The receiving phone takes it only if it has no card of its own, so nobody's medical details get replaced.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet16": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet17": "App settings that are not tied to a specific phone — such as theme, accent color, default country, quick replies, and call-handling options.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet17": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle5": "What is never synced",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle5": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet18": "Ringtones. A ringtone points at a file on the sending phone, which would not exist on the other phone.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet18": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet19": "SIM-specific settings, such as the default SIM and per-SIM ringtones or colors. These refer to the physical SIM cards in the sending phone.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet19": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle6": "Nothing on the receiving phone is deleted",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle6": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet20": "Sync only adds. The receiving phone keeps all of its own data — nothing is erased or overwritten by the contacts that come in.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet20": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet21": "A contact you already have (same name and at least one shared phone number) is skipped, not duplicated. Only brand-new contacts are added, and their details and call history come across with them.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet21": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet22": "Because an existing contact is skipped, the sender's call history for that contact is not merged in — only new contacts bring their history.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet22": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncTitle7": "Your data stays private",
  "@helpP2pSyncTitle7": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet23": "The transfer happens directly between the two phones on your local Wi-Fi. Nothing is uploaded to the internet or to any server.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet23": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncBullet24": "Opening sync is protected by your device lock, because the data can include secret contacts.",
  "@helpP2pSyncBullet24": {
    "description": "Help: one bullet point in an article section. Help prose."
  },
  "helpP2pSyncFooter": "Tip: keep both phones awake and on the same Wi-Fi until the sync finishes.",
  "@helpP2pSyncFooter": {
    "description": "Help: closing tip of an article. Help prose."
  },

  "helpFaqTroubleshootingText": "FAQs & Troubleshooting",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingText": {
    "description": "Help: text in an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingIntro": "Find quick answers to common questions about permissions, default dialer setup, privacy, sync options, and troubleshooting steps in ContactSphere.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingIntro": {
    "description": "Help: lead paragraph of an article. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle1": "General & Permissions",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle1": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ1": "Why does ContactSphere need Default Phone App permission?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ1": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA1": "Android requires an app to be set as the Default Phone App to show incoming call alerts, enable conference merging/call swap, and automatically screen and block spam calls.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA1": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ2": "Are my contacts uploaded to external servers?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ2": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA2": "No. ContactSphere is built with an offline-first architecture. All contacts, call logs, notes, and photos reside in your encrypted local SQLite database. No data is sent to external servers unless you explicitly configure your personal Google Drive / WebDAV cloud backup.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA2": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ3": "Why are some permissions optional?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ3": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA3": "Permissions such as Bluetooth (for nearby sharing), Camera (for QR and business-card scanning), and Microphone (for dictating call notes) are asked for only when you first use that feature. Refusing one disables just that feature. See the \"Permissions explained\" guide for the full list.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA3": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle2": "Dialer & Calling",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle2": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ4": "How do I search Malayalam or Devanagari names on T9?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ4": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA4": "Press the keys for the consonant group, or type the name as it sounds in English (typing 2-6-4-5 matches both \"Anil\" and \"അനിൽ\"). To change which script the keypad shows, use the \"Dialpad script\" card on the main Settings page.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA4": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ5": "How do I choose which SIM to call from?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ5": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA5": "On dual-SIM phones the dialer gives you separate SIM 1 and SIM 2 call buttons. To stop choosing every time, set a default SIM under Settings → SIM & calling → SIM Cards & Accounts, or switch on \"Ask before each call\" there.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA5": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ6": "Why didn't a call ring during quiet hours?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ6": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA6": "Quiet hours silence everything except the people you allow. Open Settings → SIM & calling → Relationship-tier quiet hours and add whoever should still get through — starred contacts, whole relationship categories, a tag, or named individuals. Anyone not on that list is silenced until the quiet hours end.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA6": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle3": "Sync, Cloud & Backups",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle3": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ7": "What is the difference between Local Wi-Fi Sync and Cloud Sync?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ7": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA7": "Local Wi-Fi sync copies data straight from one phone to another on the same network, with no internet and no account. Online sync and cloud backup use accounts you add yourself — Google, Microsoft, or a CardDAV/WebDAV server — and are off until you set one up.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA7": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ8": "What happens if I forget my Backup password?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ8": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA8": "A backup file is encrypted with the password you chose, and the app never stores it. There is no server to ask, so a lost password means the file cannot be opened. Write it down somewhere safe before you need it.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA8": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ9": "Will syncing with my phone contacts delete anything?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ9": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA9": "Standard sync merges new and updated contacts safely. Destructive / Mirror sync will warn you explicitly before replacing or removing any contacts.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA9": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle4": "Privacy & Secret Contacts",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle4": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ10": "How do I restore access if biometric unlock fails?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ10": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA10": "The phone's own unlock prompt falls back to your screen-lock PIN, pattern, or password. If you use an App PIN instead and have forgotten it, tap \"Forgot PIN?\" on the lock screen and enter the recovery code you were given when you set it up.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA10": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ11": "Why does the screen go black when switching apps?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ11": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA11": "Screenshot Guard protects sensitive views from being captured in Android's recent apps preview or by background recording tools.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA11": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle5": "Troubleshooting & Maintenance",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingTitle5": {
    "description": "Help: title (article title, topic card title or section heading). Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ12": "Search is slow or not finding new contacts. How to fix?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ12": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA12": "Open Settings → Contacts → Contact counts & search index. If any contacts have stale search keys, a Rebuild button appears — tap it and the keys are rebuilt in a few seconds.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA12": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ13": "A blocked number still shows in Recents. Is it ringing?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ13": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA13": "No. A blocked call is rejected before your phone rings, but it is still written into Recents with a \"Blocked\" mark so you can see that someone tried. If you would rather see the call and just not be disturbed, use \"Filter suspected spam\" instead of blocking.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA13": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ14": "A contact vanished on its own. Why?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ14": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA14": "It was probably saved as an ephemeral (temporary) contact, which deletes itself after 2 hours, 24 hours, 7 days, or one call. Opening such a contact shows a countdown banner with a \"Keep Permanently\" button.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA14": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ15": "Where are groups and tags?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ15": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA15": "Groups are behind the group icon in the top bar of the Contacts tab. Tags have their own tab at the bottom of the app, drawn as a cloud where a tag used by more people appears larger.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA15": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingQ16": "How do I clean up duplicate contacts?",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingQ16": {
    "description": "Help: an FAQ question. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingA16": "Open the Contacts tab, tap the three-dot menu, and choose \"Find Duplicates\". Matching is by phone number and by name (including transliterated names). Review each set, then merge it, or use \"Merge all sets\".",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingA16": {
    "description": "Help: the answer to the FAQ question with the same number. Help prose."
  },
  "helpFaqTroubleshootingFooter": "Still stuck? Open the matching guide in Help, or check Settings → Permissions to see whether the feature is simply missing a permission.",
  "@helpFaqTroubleshootingFooter": {
    "description": "Help: closing tip of an article. Help prose."
  },

